  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "AstraFlow 2.4.0:\n      - Adds the standalone AstraFlow.Assertions package for framework-neutral consumer tests.\n      - Keeps the assertion package independent from AstraFlow runtime and test-runner packages.\n      - Adds equality, nullability, string, collection, type, enum, GUID, range, and sync/async exception assertions.\n      - Adds predicate and multiple-item sequence membership, key lookup on key-value-pair sequences, and ordinal exception message pattern checks.\n      - Adds exact sequence runtime-type checks and optional reason text for equality assertions.\n      - Adds exact and assignable runtime-type checks for sequence items, including typed generic chaining and runtime-Type overloads.\n      - Adds one-pass indexed sequence-item checks with returned item access and safe failures.\n      - Adds immediate predecessor and successor sequence checks with first-match, one-pass behavior and value-safe failures.\n      - Adds lazy expected-sequence overloads and negative ordered/consecutive containment checks.\n      - Adds ascending and descending sequence-order checks by key, with one selector call per item and optional comparers.\n      - Adds structural-equivalency membership, negative membership, and all-item sequence checks with per-call options and one-pass nested snapshots.\n      - Adds ordered subsequence assertions, subject access for captured results, and reference-identity checks.\n      - Adds safe exception-chain inspection, runtime type overloads, and single-invocation exception predicates.\n      - Adds synchronous and asynchronous ArgumentException parameter-name assertions with value-safe failures.\n      - Adds bounded completion and non-completion checks for existing task completion sources, with generic result capture and assertion-only cancellation.\n      - Adds compile-checked typed property-value selection for reference subjects, including nested paths and single getter evaluation.\n      - Adds namespace-aware XML structure and deep equivalency checks for document roots, direct children, attributes, and text.\n      - Adds non-consuming HTTP response status and response/content-header checks with exact value matching.\n      - Adds opt-in public instance-field comparison to structural object-graph equivalency.\n      - Adds path-based object-graph member selection with explicit missing-path failures.\n      - Adds metadata-only type assertions for inheritance, interfaces, public properties, method overloads, and constructors.\n      - Adds exact runtime-Type equality and negative dictionary entry checks for key/value pairs and single-pass predicates.\n      - Adds exact byte-content stream assertions with bounded-memory reads, value-safe failures, and seekable-position restoration.\n      - Adds set-based collection subset/intersection checks, inclusive count bounds, and null-item checks.\n      - Adds order-independent dictionary mapping equality and inequality with default key/value equality and value-safe failures.\n      - Adds read-only syntax-based CLI analysis for assertion migration candidates, with review classifications and privacy-safe locations.\n      - Adds synchronous and asynchronous function assertion entry points for value-returning delegates.\n      - Uses safe failure messages that avoid rendering arbitrary object values and string contents by default.\n      - Adds generated mapping support for inherited entity properties, nullable scalar values, and record/primary-constructor DTOs.\n      - Full changelog: https://github.com/seifmoustafa/AstraFlow/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\n      - GitHub releases: https://github.com/seifmoustafa/AstraFlow/releases",
